help is on its way but it's coming in  bit by bit  getting vital supplies to these remote  areas of eastern afghanistan is clearly  a challenge in itself but it's needed  now more than ever  after a plea for help to the  international community humanitarian  assistance was sent by south korea  pakistan and india with more pledged  it's not only these two provinces of  ghost and bhagtika but there have also  been floodings throughout afghanistan  and many districts have been affected  afghans are facing huge problems now  in the capital kabul they're loading up  all they can to send to the areas  affected but the government here said  they don't have enough  for many countries there is a real  resistance to deal directly with the  taliban instead they say they'll send  support via aid agencies a combination  of a poor track record on human rights  and freedoms with a lack of  infrastructure means supporting  afghanistan in a time of need is proving  difficult  whatever they do have has to battle  challenging terrain and patchy  communications to get to those who need  it  it's only just over 100 miles away but  getting here from kabul can take a whole  day  and once here this is the scene  with homes reduced to rubble people are  left with no choice other than to sleep  on the ruins of where their beds once  lay  our people are very weak financially and  they don't have work  even in the next 20 years they won't be  able to rebuild their houses because of  the financial crisis we're calling on  our government and other international  organizations like ngos to help us  but in these disasters it's always the  children who suffer  officials believe over a hundred have so  far been killed and those who survived  have now lost everything  including their family  this devastation is of course down to  tuesday's rumbling earthquake but this  was a government simply not prepared and  so as they wait for more aid the taliban  will no doubt have to reflect on how  they can engage with the rest of the  world in the future to ensure when help  is needed once more they're not  abandoned again in zaman rashid sky news  in kabul
 

